{# Widget "decisions" — what needs somebody to act, and WHICH.

   THE FIGURES SAY HOW MANY; THIS SAYS WHICH, and the design puts it first
   under them for that reason.

   THREE KINDS OF PROBLEM, THREE ROWS, never one red list: a missing check-in,
   a claim the device disagrees with, and a hole are acted on by different
   people in different ways, and collapsing them hides which one anybody can
   do something about.

   THE CARD IS BOUNDED. It shows the first few and says how many there were —
   a dashboard card never grows with its data. #}
<div class="c">
    <span class="tab">Needs a decision<span class="src">&middot; {{ decisions|length }} item{{ decisions|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span></span>
    {% if decisions|length > rosterDecisionLimit %}
        <a class="more" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::TODAY_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">{{ rosterDecisionLimit }} of {{ decisions|length }} &middot; view all &rarr;</a>
    {% endif %}

    {% for row in decisions|slice(0, rosterDecisionLimit) %}
        <div class="rset">
            <span class="lb"><b>{{ row.who }}</b><em>{{ row.where }}</em></span>
            <span class="ct"><span class="r-sh {{ row.tone }}"><i></i>{{ row.kindLabel }}</span></span>
            <span class="why">{{ row.fact }}</span>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <div class="rfrag"><b>Nothing is waiting on anybody</b><em>every watch due today has been reported and the pings bear out every claim at a post</em></div>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
